From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:51:31 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] bios-dumps-off-shelf

A file whose name starts with "[BIOS]" (the No-Intro and Redump mark
for a system card, boot ROM or console firmware dump) is never a cart:
the scan skips it on every shelf, so a TurboGrafx-16 System Card, the
Lynx boot ROM or the Neo Geo Pocket Color BIOS kept beside the games no
longer shows up as a game. Lynx still reads its boot ROM from
BIOS/lynxboot.img, which the scan never looks at.
